2. DARA benchmark scans (CC BY 4.0)

data/workbench/cases/DEV001/DEV001.xy and data/workbench/cases/DEV006/DEV006.xy,
and the DEV006 scan inside launcher/demo/phaseeval-demo.tar.xz, are a subset of
the DARA benchmark data:

  Fei, McDermott, Rom, Wang and Ceder. Supplementary data for the Dara paper.
  Zenodo record 17410051 (2025).
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.17410051
  License: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

  Paper: Chemistry of Materials 38, 1364 (2026),
  https://doi.org/10.1021/acs.chemmater.5c02820

Changes: two scans selected, converted from PANalytical .xrdml to two-column
.xy (2-theta in degrees, counts), and renamed to case ids. The values are
otherwise unchanged.


3. Precursor Genome scan (CC BY 4.0)

data/workbench/cases/DEV102/DEV102.xy, and the same scan and its synthesis
record fields inside launcher/demo/phaseeval-demo.tar.xz, come from the
Precursor Genome release:

  Walters, McDermott, Rendy, Fei and Ceder (Lawrence Berkeley National
  Laboratory). Precursor Genome raw scans and ledger. Zenodo record 21285546. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21285546
  Ledger: https://github.com/lauren-walters/precursor-genome
  License: CC BY 4.0, https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

Changes: one scan selected, converted to two-column .xy and renamed to a case
id. Synthesis fields (precursors, masses, heating) were copied from the ledger
into the case record.


4. Crystallography Open Database structures (CC0)

The candidate crystal structures inside launcher/demo/phaseeval-demo.tar.xz
come from the Crystallography Open Database, https://www.crystallography.net/cod/.
COD data are dedicated to the public domain (CC0). Each CIF keeps its
_cod_database_code and the citation of the original publication. Please cite
the original authors of any structure you use.


5. Materials Project values (CC BY 4.0)

Energy-above-hull values shown by the chemistry panel and stored in the
snapshots come from the hull tables that the dara-xrd package bundles, which
are derived from the Materials Project (https://materialsproject.org).
Materials Project data are licensed CC BY 4.0. Cite: A. Jain et al., "The
Materials Project: A materials genome approach to accelerating materials
innovation", APL Materials 1, 011002 (2013).


6. BGMN (not included)

BGMN (Rietveld refinement program by J. Bergmann, http://www.bgmn.de) is not
included in this repository. PhaseEval downloads it on first use from the
mirror that DARA uses. BGMN keeps its own terms.
